  "brief": "Global Payments deal with CD&R terminated, while easyJet takeover by Apollo awaits regulatory approval, as several other deals move forward with announcements.\n\nCD&R / Global Payments (Terminated): CD&R and Global Payments Deal Terminated. CD&R and Global Payments deal has been terminated [1, 2, 3]. The deal was reportedly put on hold as CD&R and GTCR stepped back [3, 5, 7]. The termination follows earlier reports of CD&R exploring a potential $40bn take-private deal for Global Payments [4, 6, 7].\nInstalled Building Products / Old Dominion Group (Completed): Installed Building Products Acquires Old Dominion Group. Installed Building Products has acquired Old Dominion Group [8, 9, 10]. The deal is completed [8, 9, 10].\nApollo / easyJet (Pending approval): easyJet takeover by Apollo. easyJet shareholders have approved Apollo's £5.7 billion takeover bid [11, 12, 13]. The deal is now pending approval from regulatory authorities [14].\nHancock Whitney / Trustmark (Announced): Hancock Whitney and Trustmark Merger. Hancock Whitney and Trustmark are merging [15, 16]. The merger is set to be completed in early 2027 [17]. No new information is available [15, 16, 17].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Announced): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is buying Momentum Midstream for $5.5 billion [18, 19]. The deal was announced by Williams [18, 19].\nKomatsu / Astec (Announced): Komatsu to Acquire Astec. Komatsu is acquiring Astec for $75M [20]. The deal is aimed at expanding Komatsu's presence in the paving market [20]. No further details on the deal have been announced [20].\nBon Secours Mercy Health / Surgery Partners (Announced): Bon Secours Mercy Health and Surgery Partners Deal. Bon Secours Mercy Health is acquiring Surgery Partners for a reported $6 billion valuation [21, 23, 24]. The deal was initially reported to be worth $5.7 billion [22, 25]. Bon Secours has agreed to buy Surgery Partners for $5.7 billion [26, 27].\nBlueMatrix / Aiera (Announced): BlueMatrix Acquires Aiera. BlueMatrix acquires Aiera for governed research delivery to AI systems [28]. The deal was announced on November 12 [28].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- FSR Remedies Take Shape: Lessons From JD.com/CECONOMY [29].\n- Serco to buy QinetiQ U.S. for $292M [30].\n- SpaceX-Tesla merger: 3 things to know about Musk's control and the deal's size [31].",
